.TH INTRO 7
.SH NAME
intro \- SIEOS, and how this manual is laid out
.SH DESCRIPTION
SIEOS is a small, fast microkernel operating system written from scratch in
C, for x86-64 and AArch64 (QEMU, the Raspberry Pi 4 and 5, PCs from a USB
key).
It has its own file system (SieFS), its own C compiler (sicc), a desktop
laid out as BeOS's was, its own network stack with TLS 1.3 and 1.2, and an
assistant (sia) that runs a language model on the machine or talks to an
online service.
.PP
The kernel does only what nothing else can do: memory, processes and
threads, scheduling, time, signals, message passing, and interrupts
delivered as messages.
Everything else is done by ordinary programs, the servers, which talk with
messages: the console, the disk, the files, the network, users, the desktop.
A bug in a server kills only that server, and the supervisor starts it
again.
